    "conclusions": [
      "Re-reading one chunk costs 166.0 ms, the same at every setting ([166.4, 167.1, 164.5] ms), against a baseline of 102.4 ms to capture a chunk. That works out to 442.8 KiB/s for the re-read, below the 639 KiB/s of a plain SD read, because each sample also seeks and CRCs.",
      "Measured time cost: 22.2% at sample_readback=8, 5.6% at 32, 1.3% at 128. The simple model (cost per sample / (baseline chunk time x N)) reproduces them and projects 2.5% at 64 and 0.6% at 256.",
      "On the T7 capture (26.7 minutes) that is about 0.3 minutes at N=128 and 0.7 at N=64.",
      "What it buys: at N=128 it re-reads and compares 0.8% of the chunks. That is a smoke test for a card that is failing systematically, not a verification of the dump; only the PC check (or end_readback=on) covers every byte.",
      "resume_check=size finished in 3.8 ms against a full prefix re-read, as designed, and as documented it cannot detect a corrupted prefix."
    ]
